Chapter 10, Section 16: "Treachery"

"—Subaru is—"

"—an Archbishop of Sin?"

It was a suspicion that made absolutely no sense.

Even when it was spoken aloud again, as if to confirm it, it still made no sense whatsoever. It was so nonsensical that he almost wanted to laugh—if the goal was to catch them off guard, it was a resounding success.

But the expression on the face of the giant of a man before him—the one called Marcos—was far too stern to simply laugh off this incomprehensible suspicion as a joke.

At the very least, in this man’s presence, Garfiel, entrusted with the position of the camp’s chief military officer, had not a single option that involved relaxing his guard.

"..."

With a small sniff, Garfiel quietly took in the heavy tension hanging in the royal guesthouse. What he felt was suppressed fighting spirit, along with unease and distrust shaking their emotions, and behind those, the sharp, pungent scent of fear.

Garfiel knew that scent all too well; it was the same air he’d had several chances to sniff in the Vollachia Empire recently—the air of a fire magic stone storehouse just before an explosion.

In other words—

"You lot mean to throw down with us?"

"—Does that mean you are rejecting our request?"

"Hah? You come in sprayin' spit like that, pickin' a fight, and now ya make a face like we’re the ones startin' trouble?!"

"Wait. Don't bite their heads off, Garfiel. Please."

Gnashing his fangs in irritation, Garfiel glared up at the much taller Marcos—only to be reined in from behind by Emilia's words.

With her adding "please" like that, Garfiel had no choice but to pull in his horns. Emilia added a quick "thank you" for his compliance before lifting her face with firm resolve.

"I'm sorry for my companion. He just got very, very surprised and couldn’t say a word, so he got angry on my behalf."

"So Lady Emilia, are you angry as well?"

"That’s… yes, I suppose so. After getting over my initial shock at such an absurd question, I’m feeling extremely conflicted. I think I could burst out in anger any moment. But—"

Emilia stopped speaking there and placed a hand on her chest. She toyed with the green magic crystal hanging there, using its hard texture to sort through her thoughts before continuing.

"—even if I throw a tantrum here, it won't do anything to improve Subaru’s position. That would just be me getting angry for the sake of being angry. I don't think that’s right."

"...You say that plainly, looking me right in the eye."

"It had been a while since I last spoke with you, Sir Marcos. The me right now is like this—just a tiny bit stronger than before. And that's all thanks to Subaru."

"..."

Marcos narrowed his eyes at Emilia’s response—not swept away by emotion, yet not backing down either—with an expression that suggested he had much on his mind.

Meanwhile, Garfiel could feel the blood that had rushed to his head slowly cooling as he listened to Emilia speak. Even so, the tension in his body wouldn’t dissolve. Or rather, he wouldn’t let it.

"To begin with, this suspicion of yours seems utterly preposterous. Sir Natsuki connected to the Witch Cult? And at the level of an Archbishop? It’s not even a laughing matter."

"That's right! Besides, Master Subaru has personally resolved so many problems caused by the Witch Cult! He’s even defeated Archbishops, and saved me and everyone in the village... Please don't say such strange things!"

Supporting fire arrived from Otto and Petra, and Garfiel nodded enthusiastically in agreement.

After all, Subaru had led the battles that defeated or captured the Archbishops of 'Sloth,' 'Greed,' and even 'Gluttony,' dealing massive blows to the Witch Cult. In addition, Subaru had made great contributions to the subjugation of the Three Great Demon Beasts—the 'White Whale' and the 'Great Rabbit.'

To claim Subaru was involved with the Witch Cult was simply far too ridiculous.

"Oy, ya better not be sayin' we're at each other's throats 'cause we're on the same side. Even if me an' Bro Otto got into a fight, I wouldn't beat 'im to a pulp. Not that we'd ever fight in the first place."

"Whether comparing yourself to Otto is appropriate is debatable, but I, too, think that’s a fair question. ...I can’t imagine that man capable of harboring that kind of malice."

"That's right. Sure, the big brother does have a habit of trying to shoulder a mountain of trouble, but I'm pretty sure the biggest reason for that is that he just doesn't think things through."

Despite the barb tacked on by Rem, Meili, who followed up after her, was also in agreement. The camp’s opinion aligned with Garfiel’s—this was their consensus, centered around Emilia.

Receiving this, Marcos remained as stone-faced as ever.

"I understand that the members of your camp place immense trust in the knight Natsuki Subaru. That said, I request once again that Lady Emilia accompany us to the castle."

"Should I just tell the people at the castle what we talked about?"

"In addition to that, if you could answer our questions truthfully and without omission... If you'll forgive the unsolicited advice, I must tell you that your fullest cooperation in clearing up these suspicions is the surest way to dispel them."

"..."

"—Um, may I say something?"

As Emilia was lowering her violet eyes thoughtfully at Marcos, who repeated his initial demand, it was Rem who spoke up.

Like Garfiel, she was questioning him while keeping a sharp watch on the surrounding royal soldiers.

Her question was—

"What about the person at the center of this... Natsuki Subaru? Does he not need to be present?"

In that instant, the atmosphere among the royal soldiers shifted completely at her question.

"..."

The direction of the ambient emotions turned sharp, making Garfiel’s hairs stand on end.

Though no weapons were physically drawn, the sensation was akin to having the tips of swords pointed at them, and that focused attention dominated the guest hall. It was as if a barely still water surface had been trampled, causing ripples of emotion that wouldn’t fade.

It was a volatile, hair-trigger situation, where the bursting of a single bubble or a single stray droplet could set everything off—

"—Silence."

Those many wavering emotions were swept away in a single stroke by those words—or rather, by the fierce sword aura that accompanied them, forcibly subduing the rising tide.

"—!"

Garfiel felt a sensation like being struck by a palm as massive as a mountain. His pores opened in an instant reaction, and he had to use all his reason to suppress his body’s instinctive shift toward beastly transformation.

What he had felt just before, from the royal soldiers, was nothing compared to this immense sword aura. It was an extraordinary power from its source, and Garfiel’s instincts were screaming a warning.

"My soldiers were extremely discourteous. To the military officer over there—I must apologize once more for the rudeness."

"...Hah? Just me?"

"I had intended to focus it solely on my soldiers, but you were caught in it. You must be exceptionally well-trained."

As Marcos bowed his head in a slight salute, Garfiel noticed that the rest of his camp companions were frowning with puzzled faces, as if they hadn’t felt the sword aura at all.

It seemed Marcos was telling the truth—the only ones who had felt it were Garfiel and the originally intended targets, the royal soldiers. This served as a stark reminder to Garfiel.

Marcos Gildark—overshadowed by the sheer anomaly that is the 'Sword Saint' Reinhard van Astrea, but the man at the top of the Kingdom of Lugunica’s knight order—his power was no sham.

"...The way you all reacted just now seemed very, very strange to me. Won't you answer Rem's question? Where are Subaru and Beatrice?"

Setting aside Garfiel, whose jade eyes held both awe and wariness, Emilia’s eyes narrowed thoughtfully as she asked. Marcos’s expression grew a shade darker.

"...Lady Emilia, you were aware of the knight Natsuki Subaru’s movements today?"

"He went out today, saying he had a meeting with Sir Microtoff. Alone... well, with Beatrice, so the two of them. But he said he had an appointment, so..."

"Lord Microtoff McMahon is dead."

"—Huh?"

The statement, interjected as if cutting off Emilia’s words, carried an impact far greater than the bluntness of its delivery, striking the air of the room with a sharp blow.

Of course, Garfiel knew the name Microtoff McMahon.

Not just because Subaru and the others went to meet him—he was a major figure connected to the Royal Selection. Hearing of the death of someone so central to the Council of Elders... there was no way they wouldn't be shocked.

But the true shock came from the words that followed.

As Garfiel and the others were still gripped by confusion, Marcos pressed on relentlessly.

It was—

"Currently, the Kingdom is pursuing the theory that the knight Natsuki Subaru and Duke Crusch Karsten—a fellow royal candidate—conspired together and were involved in Lord McMahon’s death, and we are tracking their whereabouts."

"Wait! What does that mean? Subaru and Lady Crusch? Involved in Sir Microtoff's death...?"

"The sword wounds recovered from Lord McMahon’s body were matched to a knight’s sword bearing the crest of House Karsten. There are also reports that Lord McMahon died by Lady Karsten’s hand, and that the knight Natsuki Subaru aided in her escape."

"Wha...!"

Reeling from the sheer, methodically presented barrage of information, Garfiel felt momentarily dizzy.

Not only had the key figure Microtoff been killed, but it had been done by Crusch, with Subaru assisting her? It was nothing short of an absurd, outrageous accusation.

"Th-That Duchess...?"

Even setting aside the ridiculous suspicion leveled at Subaru, Garfiel couldn’t believe that Crusch was suspected of such a violent act.

His personal connection with Crusch only spanned a single day and a half at the Watergate City. But she was a comrade who had stood shoulder to shoulder with him in that battle, who fought the Witch Cult alongside them to save the city.

He knew she was someone who could genuinely swing a sword for someone else’s sake, and he understood the price she had paid for it—he had truly hoped something could be done for her.

Though he hadn’t met her personally, when he heard that Crusch’s body had been healed through the sacred rites of the 'Dragon Church of the Divine Dragon,' he had set aside all the complicated circumstances surrounding the Royal Selection and simply felt relieved that she was okay.

—And now, for that same Crusch to commit such an atrocity, with Subaru as her accomplice... what utter nonsense.

"—Let me confirm something. The fact that you’re tracking their whereabouts means that Sir Natsuki and Lady Crusch are still at large, correct?"

Abruptly, a question flew out from a voice that had suppressed its emotions—seeking to properly assess the current situation. The speaker, of course, was the camp’s intellectual cornerstone, Otto.

Emilia’s violet eyes, still wrestling with her shock, turned toward Otto.

"Otto..."

"It’s important. The reason the knight commander took the trouble to come here personally is less out of respect for Lady Emilia and more out of a precautionary measure, I’d wager."

"Precaution? You mean you think Lady Emilia and the rest of us might act out?"

"I won't say that possibility is zero, but the chief concern is a rendezvous. They're positioned to guard against the possibility that Sir Natsuki and the others might link up with us and be hidden here. Am I wrong?"

"Explaining the intent behind our deployment involves military secrets. I cannot answer."

"I see. That's enough, as long as you aren't denying it."

Hearing Otto nod at Marcos’s reply, Garfiel, who was struggling to knead the welling passion and turmoil inside him into something harmless, could only feel a deep sense of reliance.

At times like this, he truly felt grateful to have Otto here.

In a complex situation where multiple agendas intertwine, Garfiel trusted Otto to sort things out skillfully and provide the necessary information. Because of that, he could focus on his role as the shield.

Here too, Garfiel decided to stick to that resolve, refusing to let extraneous emotions cloud his judgment.

"The death of Lord McMahon... and the suspicion that that man might be a member of the Witch Cult... They seem related, but also not. To summon Lady Emilia to the castle to talk under these circumstances seems rather—"

"As I’ve already stated, the best way to dispel suspicion is to come to the royal castle and respond to questioning. Should you refuse, we will be forced to conclude that Lady Emilia and her camp have abandoned their responsibility to explain regarding the suspicious matters surrounding the knight Natsuki Subaru."

"That’s practically coercion, completely ignoring Lady Emilia’s will!"

"It is not coercion. However, if you refuse to comply, the suspicion will remain as suspicion, and the Kingdom will simply decide on its stance toward the knight Natsuki Subaru."

"..."

With his deep voice stripped of emotion, Marcos continued to repeat his unwavering request.

Neither push nor pull would budge him—he was as immovable as the mountain his physique suggested.

An irritated atmosphere was beginning to spread among both sides, threatening to boil over, when—

"...Understood. I will go to the castle. I’ll speak about Subaru there."

"A wise decision."

"...In that case, I'll get ready right away."

Marcos nodded to Emilia, who, rejecting both stagnation and breakdown of the situation, had resolved to comply with the demand. Despite harboring antipathy toward his attitude in her eyes, Petra began to move to prepare for the trip to the castle.

However, Otto stopped her with a "No." He narrowed his eyes, gave the wide-eyed Petra an understanding nod, and then said—

"We will carefully select who accompanies her to the castle. ...Isn't that right?"

"Perceptive. That speeds things along."

"...What does that mean?"

As Otto and Marcos exchanged glances, Emilia furrowed her finely shaped brows. To her question, Marcos straightened his tall frame to its full height and answered.

"Regarding Lady Emilia’s visit to the castle, you will not be permitted to bring your camp members with you. As it stands now, the suspicion surrounding the knight Natsuki Subaru could easily extend to Lady Emilia’s entire camp. In order to preserve the independence of the testimony, you are to be accompanied by only a single attendant, tasked solely with seeing to your personal needs."

"Just one attendant...?!"

"We regret the inconvenience, but we ask for your cooperation."

Likely having anticipated their shock, Marcos’s stance remained unchanging.

Garfiel glanced at Otto. From the slight furrow in his brow, he could tell that his older brother figure had foreseen this outcome as well. The problem was that even if it was expected, this was still a painful blow for the camp.

"At least let me, just me, be the one—"

"That is not recommended. I understand your desire to serve as her military escort, but you are more than capable as immediate combat power. Should Lady Emilia, who is currently under a cloud of suspicion, arrive at the castle accompanied by combat strength, it will be seen not as a bid to clear her name, but as a show of force."

"Tha's a damn accusation—"

"I am saying there will be those who interpret it as such."

Words were layered upon words, the other side pressing down on their intentions and keeping them in check. They wanted to somehow outmaneuver him, but the fact that even Otto wasn’t interjecting meant the opponent’s logic was sound.

But—

"When ya talk about an attendant to see to her..."

The only possible choices, given the camp’s current state, were Petra and Rem. Had Frederica been here, entrusting this to the elder sister would have been the best course—but wishing for what they didn’t have was pointless.

Leaving Emilia in the care of Rem, whose 'Memories' hadn’t returned, would be difficult. And while Petra was sharp, entrusting her with such a grave situation was too anxiety-inducing.

What on earth was the best course of action? Just as he was thinking that—

"—Then it's settled. Ram will accompany Lady Emilia."

"—! Ram?!"

Garfiel’s eyes went wide at the sight of Ram appearing at the entrance of the guest hall.

Dressed in her familiar maid uniform and wearing her usual strong-willed expression, her sudden appearance caught not just Garfiel, but Emilia and the others by surprise too.

After all, she was supposed to have been essentially bedridden, recovering from the extreme overexertion that began with their journey to the Pleiades Watchtower. She wasn't even supposed to go on the planned trip to Priestella today—she was meant to stay in the capital and wait for Garfiel and the others to return.

Yet here she was, up and about, and standing regally at Emilia's side, of all things. She promptly performed a curtsy before them as they stared in stunned silence, pinching the hem of her skirt.

"I apologize for my lateness. I was diligently checking the softness of the bedsheets, and it caused me to be late in noticing our guests' arrival."

"...So, the feel of the bed... is it all right now?"

"Indeed. I would rate it as barely passing."

Ram shrugged lightly as she answered, showing no sign of fatigue on her face. However, it was obvious this was just her usual habit of hiding her burdens well, not a sign that she had fully recovered.

The exchange with Emilia just now was a perfect example—she had substituted her own physical state with the condition of the bed. Their apprehension was far from resolved.

But—

"Nee-sama..."

"Rem, I’m leaving the rest of this leftover lot to you. None of you can manage without the power of the adorable and capable Ram and Rem sisters. Well, except Petra. She’s marginally better."

"—Yes, I understand."

Rem, having somehow swallowed all her worries and anxieties for her sister, nodded in response to Ram’s words as she naturally settled into her designated role — her light blue eyes holding back the threat of tears.

Beside their exchange, Garfiel looked toward Otto. This could be interpreted as Ram acting on her own initiative. But Otto’s judgment was—

"...Yes, I think Ram is the right choice. Can we entrust Lady Emilia to you?"

"You needn't even ask. Make sure you handle your part properly, Otto. Garf too, at least make yourself useful."

"...Ain't gotta tell me twice."

While Emilia, Rem, and even Otto all respected Ram's judgment and firmly responded as those whose roles had been delegated by her, Garfiel's voice still betrayed a hint of weakness.

He was ashamed of it, but Ram simply softened her light-crimson eyes slightly and said,

"You fool,"

pushing his weakness aside with a sweetness wrapped in severity.

"—Everyone, I'm heading out. I'll clear up Subaru's misunderstanding properly, and I'll make sure everyone understands."

And so, with Ram's selection as Emilia's attendant receiving a unanimous consensus from the camp, Emilia steeled her resolve and declared her departure, her gaze sweeping over each of Garfiel and the others' faces.

To be perfectly honest, the situation was infuriatingly unreasonable.

When the atmosphere was like this, being pushed around unilaterally was a bad omen. If this were a brawl, letting the opponent do whatever they wanted from the start would mean a swift defeat.

To avoid losing, you had to see through what the opponent wanted, stop it, and then strike back with what you wanted to do.

"As always, I'm counting on all of you. I'm asking you, please."

So saying, Emilia bowed her head deeply, making her plea to her camp companions.

Though she was the head of their camp, a royal candidate, and bore proper, prestigious titles, she still unhesitatingly bowed her head to rely on others' strength.

That was exactly why Garfiel—no, why their companions felt compelled to 












......






After seeing off Emilia, who was taken to the royal castle by Marcos and his men with only Ram as her attendant, the group...

"Everyone, gather your things—just the bare essentials. We're leaving in five minutes."

...was promptly addressed by Otto, who turned to those remaining in the royal guesthouse.

They had chased away the soldiers left to keep watch over the guesthouse, saying they wanted to confer amongst themselves. The moment they were alone in the reception room, Otto made this statement, causing Garfiel's eyes to widen.

"Five minutes?! Ain't we waitin' for Lady Emilia?!"

"No. The situation doesn't allow for even a moment's delay. Between the suspicion cast on Natsuki-san and the heavy-handed approach forcing Lady Emilia to the castle... the aim is clear."

"—It's to remove them from the Royal Selection, isn't it."

"Almost certainly."

Responding to both Garfiel's question and Petra's remark, Otto's usually gentle features sharpened with keen intelligence. "Listen," he said, raising a finger.

"The timing is just too convenient. On the very day Lord McMahon summoned him, Natsuki-san gets caught up in a bloodshed incident... and to top it off, the one who supposedly dealt the blow is Lady Crusch, a fellow royal candidate. There's a massive force at work here."

"They intend to remove both Lady Emilia and the other candidate from the board at once... That man was used to achieve that, wasn't he?"

"Based on the information we have now, that's the only conclusion. As for Lady Crusch, her continuation in the Royal Selection was already in a precarious position the moment she had to rely on the 'Dragon Church of the Divine Dragon,' but..."

"Heyyy, I get that there's no end to the talking, but don't we have like, super little time to spare? If that boulder-man comes back, that'd be bad, riiight?"

It was Meili who interjected, calling a halt to the discussion that was threatening to drag on.

Playing with her braid, the little crimson scorpion on her head snapping its claws—her "boulder-man" likely referred to Marcos.

Indeed, Marcos was currently absent, having accompanied Emilia toward the royal castle. As it was, the royal guesthouse was surrounded by royal soldiers ordered to stand guard, and the remaining members of the camp were essentially placed under a genteel house arrest. But—

"If we sit around obediently, we'll run out of moves. We act before Sir Marcos returns."

"...We're going to search for that person, aren't we."

"For Natsuki-san and Lady Crusch. We need to know what happened to them, what they saw at Lord McMahon's estate. Without knowing that, we have nothing to discuss."

"Is it all right? Relying on that person."

"Even if Natsuki-san is unreliable, Beatrice-chan is with him. The one attached to him is far more dependable than the main act."

A small smile played on Otto's lips as he gave Rem a reassuring look. Rem, her brow slightly lowered, seemed to accept the consideration, even if it wasn't heartfelt relief.

Carried by this atmosphere of shared resolve to shatter their anxieties, Garfiel slapped both his cheeks with his hands.

"All right! I'm ready to roll the dice too! Bro Otto, when we disappear, what about Lady Emilia and Ram..."

"There should be no danger to them. Bypassing all manner of procedures to cause harm to Lady Emilia, a royal candidate, is not permitted. They'll abide by that rule. In any case, the moment they forced her to the castle, the opposing side's goal is fixed: to confine Lady Emilia."

"Tch, fine! Then I'll just knock every single one of these guards silly, and in the confusion—"

"—We can't."

"Hah?!"

Cracking his knuckles and rousing his fighting spirit, Garfiel found himself faced with Otto shaking his head.

Taken aback, Garfiel stared in surprise as Otto fixed him with a serious look.

"The watch soldiers are just following orders; they aren't our enemies. We want to avoid injuring them. Ideally, we won't even make them draw their swords. What we should be doing is fleeing to prove our innocence, not waging a war."

"If we cause harm, it'll worsen the position of Lady Emilia, Nee-sama... and that person."

"That's exactly it."

As Otto nodded, adjusting his hat, Garfiel ground his back teeth.

He understood. The logic made sense. But even understanding the logic, Garfiel couldn't think of a way forward from there. Of course, if Marcos returned, the guarantee of them escaping the guesthouse safely would vanish entirely.

But for now, at least, escape through sheer force was still possible. If that option was sealed, what on earth could they do...?

"I can use insects and birds to find where the guards are light. I can ask them to create diversions too. Though it's not a sure thing..."

"—In that case, I have an idea."

"Really, Petra-san?"

While Otto was proposing his usual method using his Divine Protection, Petra suddenly raised her hand, drawing a wide-eyed question from Rem.

In response, Petra clenched her small fists tight with a "Yes!"

"I'm very, very angry right now. Angry at Subaru being suspected, angry at Lady Emilia being glared at, angry at Ram-neesama being forced to push herself. So, I'm absolutely not just going to do what they say!"

"That's both scary and reliable, but... whatcha gonna do?"

"Obviously, my super-special strategy. It's Otto-san's specialty!"

"My... specialty?"

Singled out so directly, Otto tilted his head with a blank look. Meanwhile, Petra, her cheeks flushed with excitement, was brimming with confidence about this so-called strategy.

"Petra-chan, what do you plan to dooo?"

"It's something you know too, Meili-chan, and Garf-san too. Well—"

Beckoning everyone closer, Petra had them all lean in, and she boldly laid out the details of her super-special strategy.

It was—





